<title>MEXICO: MEXICO'S CCP-DOLLAR RATE DIPS IN JULY VS JUNE.</title>
<headline>MEXICO'S CCP-DOLLAR RATE DIPS IN JULY VS JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's CCP-dollar rate, the average bank term deposit cost measured in dollars, was 6.59 percent in July, compared with 6.62 percent in February, Banco de Mexico said Monday.</p>
<p>The central bank said that the rate can be used as a reference to determine the interest rate of credits denominated in dollars.</p>
<p>The monthly calculation of the CCP-dollars includes loans of foreign banks to multiple banking institutions, and financing received from various export and import development banks.</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
